42. DATABASE CONCEPT
Organize Firestore logically.
A possible structure:
users/
  {userId}

users/{userId}/conversations/
users/{userId}/messages/
users/{userId}/memories/
users/{userId}/projects/
users/{userId}/reminders/
users/{userId}/knowledge/
users/{userId}/skills/
users/{userId}/notifications/
Knowledge chunks may be structured as:
users/{userId}/knowledge/{documentId}/chunks/{chunkId}
or another architecture optimized for the selected retrieval implementation.
Choose the structure that provides:
•	Security
•	Efficient querying
•	Scalability
•	Maintainability
________________________________________
43. LOGGING AND AUDIT
For important actions, maintain an appropriate activity log.
Example:
User requested:
"Schedule meeting with Sarah."

JARVIS:
calendar.create_event

Result:
Success

Confirmation:
Required / Granted
Logs should help with:
•	Debugging
•	Security
•	Troubleshooting
•	User transparency
Do not log secrets.
________________________________________
44. COST OPTIMIZATION
Use AI models intelligently.
Do not send every simple request to the most expensive model.
Possible strategy:
Simple conversation
        ↓
DeepSeek

Complex reasoning
        ↓
Gemini

Tool execution
        ↓
Gemini/tool-calling model

Knowledge retrieval
        ↓
Search → Relevant chunks → Appropriate AI model
The architecture must allow model routing to change later.
________________________________________
45. DEVELOPMENT PRINCIPLES
Google Antigravity must:
1.	Inspect before modifying.
2.	Preserve working code.
3.	Use reusable components.
4.	Avoid duplicated logic.
5.	Keep frontend and backend responsibilities separate.
6.	Keep API secrets server-side.
7.	Use environment variables.
8.	Implement proper loading states.
9.	Implement proper error states.
10.	Validate user input.
11.	Validate uploaded files.
12.	Enforce Firebase security rules.
13.	Test integrations.
14.	Test mobile responsiveness.
15.	Test voice interaction.
16.	Test knowledge ingestion.
17.	Test knowledge retrieval.
18.	Test permission boundaries.
________________________________________
46. DO NOT FAKE FEATURES
Do not create buttons that only display:
"Coming Soon"
when the functionality is expected to be implemented.
Do not create simulated AI responses when the real API is configured.
Do not pretend a document has been learned if processing failed.
Do not claim a calendar event was created if the API request failed.
Do not claim a file was uploaded if Storage rejected it.
Every success message must correspond to a real successful operation.
________________________________________
47. IMPLEMENTATION PRIORITY
Build in the following logical order.
Phase 1 — Foundation
•	Project architecture
•	Firebase setup
•	Authentication
