48. DEFINITION OF DONE
NAD JARVIS should not be considered complete merely because the interface looks finished.
The implementation is complete when:
AI
•	JARVIS can have real conversations.
•	AI requests reach the configured model.
•	Tool/function calling works.
Memory
•	JARVIS can save and retrieve personal information.
Knowledge
•	User can upload documents.
•	Documents are stored in Firebase Storage.
•	Metadata is stored in Firestore.
•	Documents are processed.
•	Knowledge is searchable.
•	JARVIS can answer questions using stored knowledge.
•	Sources can be identified.
Skills
•	Skills are modular.
•	Skills can be called by the AI.
•	Permissions are enforced.
•	Sensitive operations require confirmation.
Productivity
•	Calendar works.
•	Reminders work.
•	Notifications work.
Files
•	Google Drive works where configured.
•	Mega works where configured.
•	External documents can be imported into the Knowledge Library.
Voice
•	Speech recognition works.
•	Text-to-speech works.
•	Text and voice conversations share context.
Security
•	Authentication works.
•	Firestore rules are enforced.
•	Storage rules are enforced.
•	API secrets are protected.
•	Unauthorized users cannot access private data.
